msgid ""
"The :meth:`~collections.somenamedtuple._asdict` method for "
":func:`collections.namedtuple` now returns a :class:`dict` instead of a "
":class:`collections.OrderedDict`. This works because regular dicts have "
"guaranteed ordering since Python 3.7. If the extra features of "
":class:`OrderedDict` are required, the suggested remediation is to cast the "
"result to the desired type: ``OrderedDict(nt._asdict())``. (Contributed by "
"Raymond Hettinger in :issue:`35864`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`~collections.somenamedtuple._asdict` pro "
":func:`collections.namedtuple` nyn vraci :class:`dict` miste "
":class:`collections.OrderedDict`. Toto funguje, protoze bezne dicts maji "
"zarucenou poradi od Pythonu 3.7. Pokud jsou potrebny extra funkce "
":class:`OrderedDict`, navrhovana oprava je pretypovat vysledek na pozadovany"
" typ: ``OrderedDict(nt._asdict())``. (Prispela Raymond Hettinger v "
":issue:`35864`.)"

