":func:`~os.path.ismount` now return ``False`` instead of raising "
":exc:`ValueError` or its subclasses :exc:`UnicodeEncodeError` and "
":exc:`UnicodeDecodeError` for paths that contain characters or bytes "
"unrepresentable at the OS level. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`33721`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :mod:`os.path`, ktere vracejici boolean vysledek jako "
":func:`~os.path.exists`, :func:`~os.path.lexists`, :func:`~os.path.isdir`, "
":func:`~os.path.isfile`, :func:`~os.path.islink` a :func:`~os.path.ismount` "
"nyn vracejici ``False`` miste vyhozeni :exc:`ValueError` nebo jeho podskupin"
" :exc:`UnicodeEncodeError` a :exc:`UnicodeDecodeError` pro cesty, ktere "
"obsahuji znaky nebo bajty nereprezentovane na urovni OS. (Prispela Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`33721`.)"

