#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1471
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
":func:`shutil.copyfile`, :func:`shutil.copy`, :func:`shutil.copy2`, "
":func:`shutil.copytree` and :func:`shutil.move` use platform-specific "
"\"fast-copy\" syscalls on Linux and macOS in order to copy the file more "
"efficiently. \"fast-copy\" means that the copying operation occurs within "
"the kernel, avoiding the use of userspace buffers in Python as in "
"\"``outfd.write(infd.read())``\". On Windows :func:`shutil.copyfile` uses a "
"bigger default buffer size (1 MiB instead of 16 KiB) and a "
":func:`memoryview`-based variant of :func:`shutil.copyfileobj` is used. The "
"speedup for copying a 512 MiB file within the same partition is about +26% "
"on Linux, +50% on macOS and +40% on Windows. Also, much less CPU cycles are "
"consumed. See :ref:`shutil-platform-dependent-efficient-copy-operations` "
"section. (Contributed by Giampaolo Rodolà in :issue:`33671`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`shutil.copyfile`, :func:`shutil.copy`, :func:`shutil.copy2`, "
":func:`shutil.copytree` a :func:`shutil.move` pouzivaji platform-specificke "
"\"fast-copy\" syscally na Linux a macOS, aby kopie souboru vice efektivne. "
"\"fast-copy\" znamena, ze kopie operace se vyskytuje v jadre, vyhybejici se "
"pouzivani userspace buffery v Pythonu jako \"``outfd.write(infd.read())``\"."
" Na Windowsu :func:`shutil.copyfile` pouziva vetsi vychozi velikost bufferu "
"(1 MiB namiste 16 KiB) a :func:`memoryview`-zalozena varianta "
":func:`shutil.copyfileobj` je pouzivana. Zrychleni pro kopii 512 MiB souboru"
" v ramci stejneho diluv je priblizne +26% na Linux, +50% na macOS a +40% na "
"Windowsu. Take je konzumovano mnohem mene CPU cyklu. Viz :ref:`shutil-"
"platform-dependent-efficient-copy-operations` sekce. (Prispel Giampaolo "
"Rodola v :issue:`33671`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1487
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
":func:`shutil.copytree` uses :func:`os.scandir` function and all copy "
"functions depending from it use cached :func:`os.stat` values. The speedup "
"for copying a directory with 8000 files is around +9% on Linux, +20% on "
"Windows and +30% on a Windows SMB share. Also the number of :func:`os.stat` "
"syscalls is reduced by 38% making :func:`shutil.copytree` especially faster "
"on network filesystems. (Contributed by Giampaolo Rodolà in :issue:`33695`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`shutil.copytree` pouziva funkci :func:`os.scandir` a vsechny kopie "
"funkce se zaviseji z ni pouzivaji cacheovane :func:`os.stat` hodnoty. "
"Zrychleni pro kopii adresare s 8000 soubory je kolem +9% na Linux, +20% na "
"Windowsu a +30% na Windowsu SMB sdruzeni. Take je pocet :func:`os.stat` "
"syscallu snizen o 38%, co :func:`shutil.copytree` obzvlaste rychleji na "
"sitovych systemech souboru. (Prispel Giampaolo Rodola v :issue:`33695`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1494
msgid ""
"The default protocol in the :mod:`pickle` module is now Protocol 4, first "
"introduced in Python 3.4.  It offers better performance and smaller size "
"compared to Protocol 3 available since Python 3.0."
msgstr ""
"Vychozim protokolem v modulu :mod:`pickle` je nyn Protokol 4, prvne zavaden "
"v Pythonu 3.4. Nudi lepsi vykon a mensim velikostim ve srovnani s Protokolem"
" 3 dostupnym od Pythonu 3.0."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1498
msgid ""
"Removed one :c:type:`Py_ssize_t` member from ``PyGC_Head``.  All GC tracked "
"objects (e.g. tuple, list, dict) size is reduced 4 or 8 bytes. (Contributed "
"by Inada Naoki in :issue:`33597`.)"
msgstr ""
"Odstranena jedne :c:type:`Py_ssize_t` clan z ``PyGC_Head``. Vse GC sledovane"
" objekty (napr. tuple, seznam, slovnik) velikost je sniena 4 nebo 8 bajtama."
" (Prispela Inada Naoki v :issue:`33597`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1502
msgid ""
":class:`uuid.UUID` now uses ``__slots__`` to reduce its memory footprint. "
"(Contributed by Wouter Bolsterlee and Tal Einat in :issue:`30977`)"
msgstr ""
":class:`uuid.UUID` nyn pouziva ``__slots__`` ke snizenemu pameti footprint. "
"(Prispeli Wouter Bolsterlee a Tal Einat v :issue:`30977`)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1505
msgid ""
"Improved performance of :func:`operator.itemgetter` by 33%.  Optimized "
"argument handling and added a fast path for the common case of a single non-"
"negative integer index into a tuple (which is the typical use case in the "
"standard library).  (Contributed by Raymond Hettinger in :issue:`35664`.)"
msgstr ""
"Zlepseny vykon :func:`operator.itemgetter` o 33%. Optimalizovany zpracovani "
"argumentu a pridat rychlu cestu pro obvykly pripad jednoho nezaporneho "
"celociselneho indexu do tuple (ktery je typicky pouziti v standardni "
"knihovne). (Prispela Raymond Hettinger v :issue:`35664`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1511
msgid ""
"Sped-up field lookups in :func:`collections.namedtuple`.  They are now more "
"than two times faster, making them the fastest form of instance variable "
"lookup in Python. (Contributed by Raymond Hettinger, Pablo Galindo, and Joe "
"Jevnik, Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`32492`.)"
msgstr ""
"Urychlen vyhledavani poli v :func:`collections.namedtuple`. Jsou nyn vise "
"nez dvakrat rychlejsi, cini je nejrychlejsi forma vyhledavani instance "
"promenne v Pythonu. (Prispeli Raymond Hettinger, Pablo Galindo a Joe Jevnik,"
" Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`32492`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1516
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"The :class:`list` constructor does not overallocate the internal item buffer"
" if the input iterable has a known length (the input implements "
"``__len__``). This makes the created list 12% smaller on average. "
"(Contributed by Raymond Hettinger and Pablo Galindo in :issue:`33234`.)"
msgstr ""
"Konstruktor :class:`list` nealokuje prebytek interni bufferu polozky, pokud "
"ma vchodni iterable znamou delku (vchod implementuje ``__len__``). Toto cini"
" vytvoreny seznam v priemeru 12% mensi. (Prispeli Raymond Hettinger a Pablo "
"Galindo v :issue:`33234`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1521
msgid ""
"Doubled the speed of class variable writes.  When a non-dunder attribute was"
" updated, there was an unnecessary call to update slots. (Contributed by "
"Stefan Behnel, Pablo Galindo Salgado, Raymond Hettinger, Neil Schemenauer, "
"and Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`36012`.)"
msgstr ""
"Zdvojenasilna rychlost zapisu class promenne. Kdyz byla aktualizovana ne-"
"dunder vlastnost, bylo zbytecne volani aktualizace slots. (Prispeli Stefan "
"Behnel, Pablo Galindo Salgado, Raymond Hettinger, Neil Schemenauer a Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`36012`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1526
msgid ""
"Reduced an overhead of converting arguments passed to many builtin functions"
" and methods.  This sped up calling some simple builtin functions and "
"methods up to 20--50%.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`23867`, "
":issue:`35582` and :issue:`36127`.)"
msgstr ""
"Snizena rezie konverze argumentu predanych mnohym vestaveny funkcim a "
"metodam. Toto urychlenilo volani nekterych jednoduchych vstaveny funkcich a "
"metod az na 20-50%. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`23867`, "
":issue:`35582` a :issue:`36127`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1531
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"``LOAD_GLOBAL`` instruction now uses new \"per opcode cache\" mechanism. It "
"is about 40% faster now.  (Contributed by Yury Selivanov and Inada Naoki in "
":issue:`26219`.)"
msgstr ""
"Instrukce ``LOAD_GLOBAL`` nyn pouziva novi \"per opcode cache\" mechanismus."
" Je to priblizne 40% rychlejsi nyn. (Prispeli Yury Selivanov a Inada Naoki v"
" :issue:`26219`.)"

