"import by mel byt proveden z :mod:`collections.abc`. Moznost importu z "
"collections byla oznacena k odstraneni v 3.8, ale byla odlozena na 3.9. (Viz"
" :gh:`81134`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1760
msgid ""
"The :mod:`!macpath` module, deprecated in Python 3.7, has been removed. "
"(Contributed by Victor Stinner in :issue:`35471`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`!macpath`, zastaraly v Pythonu 3.7, byl odstranen. (Prispela "
"Victor Stinner v :issue:`35471`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1763 ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1883
msgid ""
"The function :func:`!platform.popen` has been removed, after having been "
"deprecated since Python 3.3: use :func:`os.popen` instead. (Contributed by "
"Victor Stinner in :issue:`35345`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`!platform.popen` byla odstranena po zataralisani od Pythonu "
"3.3: pouzijte :func:`os.popen` miste. (Prispela Victor Stinner v "
":issue:`35345`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1767
msgid ""
"The function :func:`!time.clock` has been removed, after having been "
"deprecated since Python 3.3: use :func:`time.perf_counter` or "
":func:`time.process_time` instead, depending on your requirements, to have "
"well-defined behavior. (Contributed by Matthias Bussonnier in "
":issue:`36895`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`!time.clock` byla odstranena po zataralisani od Pythonu 3.3: "
"pouzijte :func:`time.perf_counter` nebo :func:`time.process_time` miste v "
"zavislosti na vasich pozadavcich, aby se definovalo spravne chovanis. "
"(Prispela Matthias Bussonnier v :issue:`36895`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1773
msgid ""
"The ``pyvenv`` script has been removed in favor of ``python3.8 -m venv`` to "
"help eliminate confusion as to what Python interpreter the ``pyvenv`` script"
" is tied to. (Contributed by Brett Cannon in :issue:`25427`.)"
msgstr ""
"Skript ``pyvenv`` byl odstranen ve prospechu ``python3.8 -m venv`` k "
"eliminaci zmatenosti toho, na jaky Python interpret je skript ``pyvenv`` "
"vyzvan. (Prispela Brett Cannon v :issue:`25427`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1777
msgid ""
"``parse_qs``, ``parse_qsl``, and ``escape`` are removed from the :mod:`!cgi`"
" module.  They are deprecated in Python 3.2 or older. They should be "
"imported from the ``urllib.parse`` and ``html`` modules instead."
msgstr ""
"``parse_qs``, ``parse_qsl`` a ``escape`` jsou odstraneny z modulu "
":mod:`!cgi`. Jsou zastaraly v Pythonu 3.2 nebo starsi. Maji byt importovany "
"z modulu ``urllib.parse`` a ``html`` miste."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1781
msgid ""
"``filemode`` function is removed from the :mod:`tarfile` module. It is not "
"documented and deprecated since Python 3.3."
msgstr ""
"Funkce ``filemode`` je odstranena z modulu :mod:`tarfile`. Neni "
"dokumentovana a zastarala od Pythonu 3.3."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1784
msgid ""
"The :class:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser` constructor no longer accepts "
"the *html* argument.  It never had an effect and was deprecated in Python "
"3.4. All other parameters are now :ref:`keyword-only <keyword-"
"only_parameter>`. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`29209`.)"
msgstr ""
"Konstruktor :class:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser` jiz neakceptuje "
"argument *html*. Nikdy nemala efekt a byla zastarala v Pythonu 3.4. Vse "
"ostatni parametry jsou nyn :ref:`keyword-only <keyword-only_parameter>`. "
"(Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`29209`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1789
msgid ""
"Removed the ``doctype()`` method of "
":class:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser`. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka "
"in :issue:`29209`.)"
msgstr ""
"Odstrany metoda ``doctype()`` :class:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser`. "
"(Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`29209`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1792
msgid ""
"\"unicode_internal\" codec is removed. (Contributed by Inada Naoki in "
":issue:`36297`.)"
msgstr ""
"\"unicode_internal\" kodek je odstranen. (Prispela Inada Naoki v "
":issue:`36297`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1795
msgid ""
"The ``Cache`` and ``Statement`` objects of the :mod:`sqlite3` module are not"
" exposed to the user. (Contributed by Aviv Palivoda in :issue:`30262`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty ``Cache`` a ``Statement`` modulu :mod:`sqlite3` nejsou vystavovany "
"uzivateli. (Prispela Aviv Palivoda v :issue:`30262`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1799
msgid ""
"The ``bufsize`` keyword argument of :func:`fileinput.input` and "
":func:`fileinput.FileInput` which was ignored and deprecated since Python "
"3.6 has been removed. :issue:`36952` (Contributed by Matthias Bussonnier.)"
msgstr ""
"Klicovy argument ``bufsize`` :func:`fileinput.input` a "
":func:`fileinput.FileInput`, ktery byl ignorovan a zastaraly od Pythonu 3.6,"
" byl odstranen. :issue:`36952` (Prispela Matthias Bussonnier.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1803
msgid ""
"The functions :func:`!sys.set_coroutine_wrapper` and "
":func:`!sys.get_coroutine_wrapper` deprecated in Python 3.7 have been "
"removed; :issue:`36933` (Contributed by Matthias Bussonnier.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`!sys.set_coroutine_wrapper` a "
":func:`!sys.get_coroutine_wrapper` zastaraly v Pythonu 3.7 byly odstrany; "
":issue:`36933` (Prispela Matthias Bussonnier.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1809
msgid "Porting to Python 3.8"
msgstr "Portovani do Pythonu 3.8"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1811
msgid ""
"This section lists previously described changes and other bugfixes that may "
"require changes to your code."
msgstr ""
"Tato sekce uvadi drivejsi popsane zmeny a ostatni opravy chyb, ktere mohou "
"vyzadovat zmeny ve vasem kodu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1816
msgid "Changes in Python behavior"
msgstr "Zmeny chovanis Pythonu"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1818
msgid ""
"Yield expressions (both ``yield`` and ``yield from`` clauses) are now "
"disallowed in comprehensions and generator expressions (aside from the "
"iterable expression in the leftmost :keyword:`!for` clause). (Contributed by"
" Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`10544`.)"
msgstr ""
"Výrazy yield (jak ``yield``, tak ``yield from`` klauzule) jsou nyní zakázány "
"v comprehensions a v generátorových výrazech (mimo výraz iterable v nejlevější "
":keyword:`!for` klauzuli). (Přispěl Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`10544`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1823
msgid ""
"The compiler now produces a :exc:`SyntaxWarning` when identity checks "
"(``is`` and ``is not``) are used with certain types of literals (e.g. "
"strings, numbers).  These can often work by accident in CPython, but are not"
" guaranteed by the language spec.  The warning advises users to use equality"
" tests (``==`` and ``!=``) instead. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`34850`.)"
msgstr ""
"Kompiln nyn produkuje :exc:`SyntaxWarning`, kdy jsou kontroly identity "
"(``is`` a ``is not``) pouzivany s urcitymi typy literalu (napr. retezce, "
"cisla). Tyto mohou casto fungovat accident v CPython, ale nejsou zaruci "
"specifikou jazyku. Varovani doporučuje uzivatele pouzit testy rovnosti "
"(``==`` a ``!='`) miste. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`34850`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1830
msgid ""
"The CPython interpreter can swallow exceptions in some circumstances. In "
"Python 3.8 this happens in fewer cases.  In particular, exceptions raised "
"when getting the attribute from the type dictionary are no longer ignored. "
"(Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`35459`.)"
msgstr ""
"Interpret CPython muze spolknout vyjimky v nekterych okolnostech. V Pythonu "
"3.8 se to stava v mensi pomoci. Konkretne vyjimky vyvolane pri ziskavani "
"atributu ze slovniku typu jsou jiz ignorovany. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v "
":issue:`35459`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1835
msgid ""
"Removed ``__str__`` implementations from builtin types :class:`bool`, "
":class:`int`, :class:`float`, :class:`complex` and few classes from the "
"standard library.  They now inherit ``__str__()`` from :class:`object`. As "
"result, defining the ``__repr__()`` method in the subclass of these classes "
"will affect their string representation. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in"
" :issue:`36793`.)"
msgstr ""
"Odstraneny ``__str__`` implementace z vstavene typy :class:`bool`, "
":class:`int`, :class:`float`, :class:`complex` a nektere tridy ze standardni"
" knihovny. Nyn dedi ``__str__()`` z :class:`object`. Jako vysledek, defini "
"metodu ``__repr__()`` v podskupine techto trid bude ovlivnit jejich retezec "
"reprezentaci. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`36793`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1842
msgid ""
"On AIX, :data:`sys.platform` doesn't contain the major version anymore. It "
"is always ``'aix'``, instead of ``'aix3'`` .. ``'aix7'``.  Since older "
"Python versions include the version number, so it is recommended to always "
"use ``sys.platform.startswith('aix')``. (Contributed by M. Felt in "
":issue:`36588`.)"
msgstr ""
"Na AIX, :data:`sys.platform` neobsahuje hlavni verzi. Je vzdy ``'aix'``, "
"miste ``'aix3'`` .. ``'aix7'``. Vzhledem k tomu, ze starsi Python verze "
"obsahuji cislo verze, doporucuje se vzdy pouzit "
"``sys.platform.startswith('aix')``. (Prispela M. Felt v :issue:`36588`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1848
msgid ""
":c:func:`!PyEval_AcquireLock` and :c:func:`!PyEval_AcquireThread` now "
"terminate the current thread if called while the interpreter is finalizing, "
"making them consistent with :c:func:`PyEval_RestoreThread`, "
":c:func:`Py_END_ALLOW_THREADS`, and :c:func:`PyGILState_Ensure`. If this "
"behavior is not desired, guard the call by checking "
":c:func:`!_Py_IsFinalizing` or :func:`sys.is_finalizing`. (Contributed by "
"Joannah Nanjekye in :issue:`36475`.)"
msgstr ""
":c:func:`!PyEval_AcquireLock` a :c:func:`!PyEval_AcquireThread` nyn ukoncuji"
" aktualni vlakno pokud je volano zatimco interpret finalizuji, cinisoci je "
"konzistentnime s :c:func:`PyEval_RestoreThread`, "
":c:func:`Py_END_ALLOW_THREADS` a :c:func:`PyGILState_Ensure`. Pokud toto "
"chovanis neni pozadovano, ostrazte volani kontrolou "
":c:func:`!_Py_IsFinalizing` nebo :func:`sys.is_finalizing`. (Prispela "
"Joannah Nanjekye v :issue:`36475`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1858 ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2324
msgid "Changes in the Python API"
msgstr "Zmeny v Python API"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1860
msgid ""
"The :func:`os.getcwdb` function now uses the UTF-8 encoding on Windows, "
"rather than the ANSI code page: see :pep:`529` for the rationale. The "
"function is no longer deprecated on Windows. (Contributed by Victor Stinner "
"in :issue:`37412`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`os.getcwdb` nyn pouziva kodovani UTF-8 na Windowsu, spise nez "
"stranku ANSI: viz :pep:`529` pro duvodpodstaty. Funkce se jiz nezvlastne na "
"Windowsu. (Prispela Victor Stinner v :issue:`37412`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1865
msgid ""
":class:`subprocess.Popen` can now use :func:`os.posix_spawn` in some cases "
"for better performance. On Windows Subsystem for Linux and QEMU User "
"Emulation, the :class:`~subprocess.Popen` constructor using "
":func:`os.posix_spawn` no longer raises an exception on errors like "
"\"missing program\".  Instead the child process fails with a non-zero "
":attr:`~subprocess.Popen.returncode`. (Contributed by Joannah Nanjekye and "
"Victor Stinner in :issue:`35537`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`subprocess.Popen` nyn muze pouzit :func:`os.posix_spawn` v nekterych"
" pripadech pro lepsi vykon. Na Windows Subsysteme pro Linux a QEMU Uzivatele"
" Emulace, konstruktor :class:`~subprocess.Popen` pouzivajici "
":func:`os.posix_spawn` jiz vyhodi vyjimku pri chybach jako \"chybejici "
"program\". Miste toho proces dite selhe s nenulovym "
":attr:`~subprocess.Popen.returncode`. (Prispeli Joannah Nanjekye a Victor "
"Stinner v :issue:`35537`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1873
msgid ""
"The *preexec_fn* argument of * :class:`subprocess.Popen` is no longer "
"compatible with subinterpreters. The use of the parameter in a "
"subinterpreter now raises :exc:`RuntimeError`. (Contributed by Eric Snow in "
":issue:`34651`, modified by Christian Heimes in :issue:`37951`.)"
msgstr ""
"Argument *preexec_fn* z *:class:`subprocess.Popen` jiz neni kompatibilni se "
"subinterpretry. Pouziti parametru v subinterpretru nyn vyhodi "
":exc:`RuntimeError`. (Prispel Eric Snow v :issue:`34651`, zmenen Christian "
"Heimes v :issue:`37951`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1879
msgid ""
"The :meth:`imaplib.IMAP4.logout` method no longer silently ignores arbitrary"
" exceptions. (Contributed by Victor Stinner in :issue:`36348`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`imaplib.IMAP4.logout` jiz tisice ignoruje libovolne vyjimky. "
"(Prispela Victor Stinner v :issue:`36348`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1887
msgid ""
"The :func:`statistics.mode` function no longer raises an exception when "
"given multimodal data.  Instead, it returns the first mode encountered in "
"the input data.  (Contributed by Raymond Hettinger in :issue:`35892`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`statistics.mode` jiz nevyhodi vyjimku pri dane multimodalni "
"datech. Miste toho vraci prvni rezim nalezeny ve vstupnich datech. (Prispela"
" Raymond Hettinger v :issue:`35892`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1892
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~tkinter.ttk.Treeview.selection` method of the "
":class:`tkinter.ttk.Treeview` class no longer takes arguments.  Using it "
"with arguments for changing the selection was deprecated in Python 3.6.  Use"
" specialized methods like :meth:`~tkinter.ttk.Treeview.selection_set` for "
"changing the selection.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`31508`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`~tkinter.ttk.Treeview.selection` tridy "
":class:`tkinter.ttk.Treeview` vyjimka jiz neprijima argumenty. Pouzivani ho "
"s argumenty pro zmenu vyber bylo zastaralo v Pythonu 3.6. Pouzij "
"specializovane metody jako :meth:`~tkinter.ttk.Treeview.selection_set` pro "
"zmenu vyberu. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`31508`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1898
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.writexml`, "
":meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.toxml` and "
":meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.toprettyxml` methods of :mod:`xml.dom.minidom` "
"and the :meth:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.ElementTree.write` method of "
":mod:`xml.etree.ElementTree` now preserve the attribute order specified by "
"the user. (Contributed by Diego Rojas and Raymond Hettinger in "
":issue:`34160`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metody :meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.writexml`, "
":meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.toxml` a "
":meth:`~xml.dom.minidom.Node.toprettyxml` :mod:`xml.dom.minidom` a metoda "
":meth:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.ElementTree.write` "
":mod:`xml.etree.ElementTree` nyn zachovavaji poradi atributu specifikovane "
"uziva. (Prispeli Diego Rojas a Raymond Hettinger v :issue:`34160`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1905
msgid ""
"A :mod:`dbm.dumb` database opened with flags ``'r'`` is now read-only. "
":func:`dbm.dumb.open` with flags ``'r'`` and ``'w'`` no longer creates a "
"database if it does not exist. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`32749`.)"
msgstr ""
"Databaze :mod:`dbm.dumb` otevrena s flagi ``'r'`` je nyn pouze pro cteni. "
":func:`dbm.dumb.open` s flagi ``'r'`` a ``'w'`` jiz vytvarnej databazi pokud"
" neexistuje. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`32749`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1910
msgid ""
"The ``doctype()`` method defined in a subclass of "
":class:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser` will no longer be called and will "
"emit a :exc:`RuntimeWarning` instead of a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. Define "
"the :meth:`doctype() <xml.etree.ElementTree.TreeBuilder.doctype>` method on "
"a target for handling an XML doctype declaration. (Contributed by Serhiy "
"Storchaka in :issue:`29209`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda ``doctype()`` definovana v podskupine "
":class:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser` jiz nebude volana a bude "
"vyzarovati :exc:`RuntimeWarning` miste :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. Definuj "
"metodu :meth:`doctype() <xml.etree.ElementTree.TreeBuilder.doctype>` na cili"
" pro zpracovani XML deklarace doctype. (Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v "
":issue:`29209`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1917
msgid ""
"A :exc:`RuntimeError` is now raised when the custom metaclass doesn't "
"provide the ``__classcell__`` entry in the namespace passed to "
"``type.__new__``.  A :exc:`DeprecationWarning` was emitted in Python 3.6--"
"3.7.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`23722`.)"
msgstr ""
":exc:`RuntimeError` je nyn vyhozena kdyz vlastni metaklas neposkytuje zapis "
"``__classcell__`` v namespace predane :c:func:`type.__new__`. "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning` byl vydana v Pythonu 3.6-3.7. (Prispela Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`23722`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1922
msgid ""
"The :class:`cProfile.Profile <profile.Profile>` class can now be used as a "
"context manager. (Contributed by Scott Sanderson in :issue:`29235`.)"
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`cProfile.Profile <profile.Profile>` nyn muze byt pouzita jako "
"context manager. (Prispela Scott Sanderson v :issue:`29235`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1925
msgid ""
":func:`shutil.copyfile`, :func:`shutil.copy`, :func:`shutil.copy2`, "
":func:`shutil.copytree` and :func:`shutil.move` use platform-specific "
"\"fast-copy\" syscalls (see :ref:`shutil-platform-dependent-efficient-copy-"
"operations` section)."
msgstr ""
":func:`shutil.copyfile`, :func:`shutil.copy`, :func:`shutil.copy2`, "
":func:`shutil.copytree` a :func:`shutil.move` pouzivaji platform-specificke "
"\"fast-copy\" syscally (viz :ref:`shutil-platform-dependent-efficient-copy-"
"operations` sekce)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1930
msgid ""
":func:`shutil.copyfile` default buffer size on Windows was changed from 16 "
"KiB to 1 MiB."
msgstr ""
"Vychozi velikost bufferu :func:`shutil.copyfile` na Windowsu byla zmenen z "
"16 KiB na 1 MiB."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1933
msgid ""
"The ``PyGC_Head`` struct has changed completely.  All code that touched the "
"struct member should be rewritten.  (See :issue:`33597`.)"
msgstr ""
"Struktura ``PyGC_Head`` se zmenila uplne. Vse kód, který se dotýkal clěnu "
"struktury by měl být přepsan. (Viz :issue:`33597`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1936
msgid ""
"The :c:type:`PyInterpreterState` struct has been moved into the \"internal\""
" header files (specifically Include/internal/pycore_pystate.h).  An opaque "
"``PyInterpreterState`` is still available as part of the public API (and "
"stable ABI).  The docs indicate that none of the struct's fields are public,"
" so we hope no one has been using them.  However, if you do rely on one or "
"more of those private fields and have no alternative then please open a BPO "
"issue.  We'll work on helping you adjust (possibly including adding accessor"
" functions to the public API).  (See :issue:`35886`.)"
msgstr ""
"Struktura :c:type:`PyInterpreterState` byla premistena do \"internih\" "
"hlavickovych souboru (konkretne Include/internal/pycore_pystate.h). "
"Nepruhledne ``PyInterpreterState`` je stale dostupne jako cast verejneho API"
" (a stabilniho ABI). Dokumenty ukazuji, ze zadne z poli struktury nejsou "
"verejne, tak doufame, ze nikdo nevyuzival. Vsak pokud spolehlivate na jednom"
" nebo vice privat polach a nemate alternativu, otevrite prosim BPO problem. "
"Budeme vam pomahat prilagodeni (mozna vcetn pridani accessor funkcich do "
"verejneho API). (Viz :issue:`35886`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1946
msgid ""
"The :meth:`mmap.flush() <mmap.mmap.flush>` method now returns ``None`` on "
"success and raises an exception on error under all platforms.  Previously, "
"its behavior was platform-dependent: a nonzero value was returned on "
"success; zero was returned on error under Windows.  A zero value was "
"returned on success; an exception was raised on error under Unix. "
"(Contributed by Berker Peksag in :issue:`2122`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`mmap.flush() <mmap.mmap.flush>` nyn vraci ``None`` pri uspechu"
" a vyhodi vyjimku pri chybe na vsech platformach. Driveji bylo jeji chovanis"
" platform-zavisle: nenulova hodnota byla vracena pri uspechu; nula byla "
"vracena pri chybe na Windowsu. Nulova hodnota byla vracena pri uspechu; "
"vyjimka byla vyhozena pri chybe na Unix. (Prispela Berker Peksag v "
":issue:`2122`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1953
msgid ""
":mod:`xml.dom.minidom` and :mod:`xml.sax` modules no longer process external"
" entities by default. (Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`17239`.)"
msgstr ""
"Moduly :mod:`xml.dom.minidom` a :mod:`xml.sax` jiz nezpracovavaji vnejsi "
"entity ve vychozim nastaveni. (Prispela Christian Heimes v :issue:`17239`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1957
msgid ""
"Deleting a key from a read-only :mod:`dbm` database (:mod:`dbm.dumb`, "
":mod:`dbm.gnu` or :mod:`dbm.ndbm`) raises :attr:`!error` "
"(:exc:`dbm.dumb.error`, :exc:`dbm.gnu.error` or :exc:`dbm.ndbm.error`) "
"instead of :exc:`KeyError`. (Contributed by Xiang Zhang in :issue:`33106`.)"
msgstr ""
"Smazani klice z databaze :mod:`dbm` pouze pro cteni (:mod:`dbm.dumb`, "
":mod:`dbm.gnu` nebo :mod:`dbm.ndbm`) vyhodi :attr:`!error` "
"(:exc:`dbm.dumb.error`, :exc:`dbm.gnu.error` nebo :exc:`dbm.ndbm.error`) "
"miste :exc:`KeyError`. (Prispela Xiang Zhang v :issue:`33106`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1962
msgid ""
"Simplified AST for literals.  All constants will be represented as "
":class:`ast.Constant` instances.  Instantiating old classes ``Num``, "
"``Str``, ``Bytes``, ``NameConstant`` and ``Ellipsis`` will return an "
"instance of ``Constant``. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`32892`.)"
msgstr ""
"Zjednodusen AST pro literaly. Vsechny konstanty budou reprezentovany jako "
"instance :class:`ast.Constant`. Instanciace starych trid ``Num``, ``Str``, "
"``Bytes``, ``NameConstant`` a ``Ellipsis`` vraci instanci ``Constant``. "
"(Prispela Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`32892`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1978
msgid ""
"The function :func:`asyncio.wait_for` now correctly waits for cancellation "
"when using an instance of :class:`asyncio.Task`. Previously, upon reaching "
"*timeout*, it was cancelled and immediately returned. (Contributed by Elvis "
"Pranskevichus in :issue:`32751`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`asyncio.wait_for` nyn spravne ceka na zruseni pri pouziti "
"instance :class:`asyncio.Task`. Driveji, po dosazen *timeout*, byla zrusena "
"a ihned vracena. (Prispela Elvis Pranskevichus v :issue:`32751`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1983
msgid ""
"The function :func:`asyncio.BaseTransport.get_extra_info` now returns a safe"
" to use socket object when 'socket' is passed to the *name* parameter. "
"(Contributed by Yury Selivanov in :issue:`37027`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`asyncio.BaseTransport.get_extra_info` nyn vraci bezpecny "
"objekt socket pri prosazhovani 'socket' do parametru *name*. (Prispela Yury "
"Selivanov v :issue:`37027`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1987
msgid ":class:`asyncio.BufferedProtocol` has graduated to the stable API."
msgstr ":class:`asyncio.BufferedProtocol` se absolvovao na stabilni API."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:1991
msgid ""
"DLL dependencies for extension modules and DLLs loaded with :mod:`ctypes` on"
" Windows are now resolved more securely. Only the system paths, the "
"directory containing the DLL or PYD file, and directories added with "
":func:`~os.add_dll_directory` are searched for load-time dependencies. "
"Specifically, :envvar:`PATH` and the current working directory are no longer"
" used, and modifications to these will no longer have any effect on normal "
"DLL resolution. If your application relies on these mechanisms, you should "
"check for :func:`~os.add_dll_directory` and if it exists, use it to add your"
" DLLs directory while loading your library. Note that Windows 7 users will "
"need to ensure that Windows Update KB2533623 has been installed (this is "
"also verified by the installer). (Contributed by Steve Dower in "
":issue:`36085`.)"
msgstr ""
"DLL zavislosti pro extension moduly a DLL nacitane s :mod:`ctypes` na "
"Windowsu jsou nyn reseny bezpecneji. Pouze cesty systemu, adresar obsahujici"
" DLL nebo PYD soubor a adresare pridane s :func:`~os.add_dll_directory` jsou"
" prohledavany pro zavislosti behem nacitani. Konkretne :envvar:`PATH` a "
"pracovni adresar jiz nejsou pouzivany a zmeny na nich nebudou mit zadny vliv"
" na normalniho rozliseni DLL. Pokud se vasa aplikace spolehuje na tyto "
"mechanismy, meli byste zkontrolovat :func:`~os.add_dll_directory` a pokud "
"existuje, pouzijte ji k pridani vaseho DLL adresare pri nacitani knihovny. "
"Poznamejte, ze uzivatele Windows 7 budou muset zajistit, ze Windows Update "
"KB2533623 byla instalovana (toto je take overovano instalatorem). (Prispela "
"Steve Dower v :issue:`36085`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2004
msgid ""
"The header files and functions related to pgen have been removed after its "
"replacement by a pure Python implementation. (Contributed by Pablo Galindo "
"in :issue:`36623`.)"
msgstr ""
"Hlavickove soubory a funkce souvisejici s pgen byly odstraneny po jeji "
"nahrade cistym Python implementaci. (Prispela Pablo Galindo v "
":issue:`36623`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2008
msgid ""
":class:`types.CodeType` has a new parameter in the second position of the "
"constructor (*posonlyargcount*) to support positional-only arguments defined"
" in :pep:`570`. The first argument (*argcount*) now represents the total "
"number of positional arguments (including positional-only arguments). The "
"new ``replace()`` method of :class:`types.CodeType` can be used to make the "
"code future-proof."
msgstr ""
":class:`types.CodeType` ma novy parametr v druhe pozici konstruktoru "
"(*posonlyargcount*) pro podporu pouze pozicnich argumentu definovany v "
":pep:`570`. Prvni argument (*argcount*) nyn predstavuje celkovy pocet "
"pozicnich argumentu (vcetn pouze pozicnich argumentu). Nova metoda "
"``replace()`` :class:`types.CodeType` muze byt pouzita k vytvoreni kodu "
"odolne voci budoucnosti."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2015
msgid ""
"The parameter ``digestmod`` for :func:`hmac.new` no longer uses the MD5 "
"digest by default."
msgstr ""
"Parametr ``digestmod`` pro :func:`hmac.new` jiz nepouziva MD5 digest ve "
"vychozim nastaveni."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2019
msgid "Changes in the C API"
msgstr "Zmeny v C API"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2021
msgid ""
"The :c:struct:`PyCompilerFlags` structure got a new *cf_feature_version* "
"field. It should be initialized to ``PY_MINOR_VERSION``. The field is "
"ignored by default, and is used if and only if ``PyCF_ONLY_AST`` flag is set"
" in *cf_flags*. (Contributed by Guido van Rossum in :issue:`35766`.)"
msgstr ""
"Struktura :c:struct:`PyCompilerFlags` dostala nove pole "
"*cf_feature_version*. Mela by byt inicializovana na ``PY_MINOR_VERSION``. "
"Pole je ignorovano ve vychozim nastaveni a je pouzivano pouze pokud je "
"vlajka ``PyCF_ONLY_AST`` v *cf_flags*. (Prispela Guido van Rossum v "
":issue:`35766`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2027
msgid ""
"The :c:func:`!PyEval_ReInitThreads` function has been removed from the C "
"API. It should not be called explicitly: use :c:func:`PyOS_AfterFork_Child` "
"instead. (Contributed by Victor Stinner in :issue:`36728`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :c:func:`!PyEval_ReInitThreads` byla odstranena z C API. Nema byt "
"volana explicitne: pouzij :c:func:`PyOS_AfterFork_Child` miste. (Prispela "
"Victor Stinner v :issue:`36728`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2032
msgid ""
"On Unix, C extensions are no longer linked to libpython except on Android "
"and Cygwin. When Python is embedded, ``libpython`` must not be loaded with "
"``RTLD_LOCAL``, but ``RTLD_GLOBAL`` instead. Previously, using "
"``RTLD_LOCAL``, it was already not possible to load C extensions which were "
"not linked to ``libpython``, like C extensions of the standard library built"
" by the ``*shared*`` section of ``Modules/Setup``. (Contributed by Victor "
"Stinner in :issue:`21536`.)"
msgstr ""
"Na Unix jsou extension C jiz propojeny s libpython krome Android a Cygwin. "
"Pokud je Python vlozen, ``libpython`` nesmí být naložen s ``RTLD_LOCAL``, "
"ale ``RTLD_GLOBAL`` miste. Driveji pri pouziti ``RTLD_LOCAL``, nebylo mozne "
"nacist extension C, ktere nebyly propojeny s ``libpython``, jako extension C"
" standardni knihovny postavene sekci ``*shared*`` ``Modules/Setup``. "
"(Prispela Victor Stinner v :issue:`21536`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2040
msgid ""
"Use of ``#`` variants of formats in parsing or building value (e.g. "
":c:func:`PyArg_ParseTuple`, :c:func:`Py_BuildValue`, "
":c:func:`PyObject_CallFunction`, etc.) without ``PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN`` defined "
"raises ``DeprecationWarning`` now. It will be removed in 3.10 or 4.0.  Read "
":ref:`arg-parsing` for detail. (Contributed by Inada Naoki in "
":issue:`36381`.)"
msgstr ""
"Pouziti ``#`` variant formatu pri analyze nebo stavba hodnoty (napr. "
":c:func:`PyArg_ParseTuple`, :c:func:`Py_BuildValue`, "
":c:func:`PyObject_CallFunction` atd.) bez ``PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN`` definovane "
"vyhodi ``DeprecationWarning`` nyn. Bude odstranena v 3.10 nebo 4.0. Precti "
":ref:`arg-parsing` pro detail. (Prispela Inada Naoki v :issue:`36381`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2046
msgid ""
"Instances of heap-allocated types (such as those created with "
":c:func:`PyType_FromSpec`) hold a reference to their type object. Increasing"
" the reference count of these type objects has been moved from "
":c:func:`PyType_GenericAlloc` to the more low-level functions, "
":c:func:`PyObject_Init` and :c:macro:`!PyObject_INIT`. This makes types "
"created through :c:func:`PyType_FromSpec` behave like other classes in "
"managed code."
msgstr ""
"Instance heap-alokove typy (jako ty vytvorene s :c:func:`PyType_FromSpec`) "
"drzi odkaz na jejich objektu typu. Zvysovani poctu odkazu techto objektu "
"typu bylo premisteno z :c:func:`PyType_GenericAlloc` na nizsi funkce, "
":c:func:`PyObject_Init` a :c:macro:`!PyObject_INIT`. Toto cini typy "
"vytvorene pres :c:func:`PyType_FromSpec` chovat se jako ostatni tridy ve "
"spravovane kodu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2054
msgid ":ref:`Statically allocated types <static-types>` are not affected."
msgstr ":ref:`Staticky alokove typy <static-types>` nejsou ovlivneny."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2056
msgid ""
"For the vast majority of cases, there should be no side effect. However, "
"types that manually increase the reference count after allocating an "
"instance (perhaps to work around the bug) may now become immortal. To avoid "
"this, these classes need to call Py_DECREF on the type object during "
"instance deallocation."
msgstr ""
"Pro rozsahlou vetsi cast pripadu by nemel byt zadny vedlejsi ucinek. Vsak "
"typy, ktere rucne zvysily pocet odkazu po alokaci instance (mozna aby se "
"obchvilo chyby) se mohou nyn stat nesmrtelnymi. Aby se tomu vyhnulo, tyto "
"tridy potrebuji volat Py_DECREF na objektu typu behem dealokace instance."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2062
msgid ""
"To correctly port these types into 3.8, please apply the following changes:"
msgstr ""
"Aby bylo spravne portovano tyto typy do 3.8, prosim aplikuj nasledujici "
"zmeny:"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2065
msgid ""
"Remove :c:macro:`Py_INCREF` on the type object after allocating an instance "
"- if any. This may happen after calling :c:macro:`PyObject_New`, "
":c:macro:`PyObject_NewVar`, :c:func:`PyObject_GC_New`, "
":c:func:`PyObject_GC_NewVar`, or any other custom allocator that uses "
":c:func:`PyObject_Init` or :c:macro:`!PyObject_INIT`."
msgstr ""
"Odstraň :c:macro:`Py_INCREF` na objektu typu po alokaci instance - pokud je."
" To se muze stat po volani :c:macro:`PyObject_New`, "
":c:macro:`PyObject_NewVar`, :c:func:`PyObject_GC_New`, "
":c:func:`PyObject_GC_NewVar` nebo jakekoli custom alokator, ktery pouziva "
":c:func:`PyObject_Init` nebo :c:macro:`!PyObject_INIT`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2072 ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2091
#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2110
msgid "Example:"
msgstr "Priklad:"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2074
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"static foo_struct *\n"
"foo_new(PyObject *type) {\n"
"    foo_struct *foo = PyObject_GC_New(foo_struct, (PyTypeObject *) type);\n"
"    if (foo == NULL)\n"
"        return NULL;\n"
"#if PY_VERSION_HEX < 0x03080000\n"
"    // Workaround for Python issue 35810; no longer necessary in Python 3.8\n"
"    PY_INCREF(type)\n"
"#endif\n"
"    return foo;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static foo_struct *\n"
"foo_new(PyObject *type) {\n"
"    foo_struct *foo = PyObject_GC_New(foo_struct, (PyTypeObject *) type);\n"
"    if (foo == NULL)\n"
"        return NULL;\n"
"#if PY_VERSION_HEX < 0x03080000\n"
"    // Workaround for Python issue 35810; no longer necessary in Python 3.8\n"
"    PY_INCREF(type)\n"
"#endif\n"
"    return foo;\n"
"}"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2088
msgid ""
"Ensure that all custom ``tp_dealloc`` functions of heap-allocated types "
"decrease the type's reference count."
msgstr ""
"Ujisti se, ze vsechny vlastni ``tp_dealloc`` funkce heap-alokoveho typu "
"snizeit pocet odkazu typu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2093
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"static void\n"
"foo_dealloc(foo_struct *instance) {\n"
"    PyObject *type = Py_TYPE(instance);\n"
"    PyObject_GC_Del(instance);\n"
"#if PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x03080000\n"
"    // This was not needed before Python 3.8 (Python issue 35810)\n"
"    Py_DECREF(type);\n"
"#endif\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static void\n"
"foo_dealloc(foo_struct *instance) {\n"
"    PyObject *type = Py_TYPE(instance);\n"
"    PyObject_GC_Del(instance);\n"
"#if PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x03080000\n"
"    // This was not needed before Python 3.8 (Python issue 35810)\n"
"    Py_DECREF(type);\n"
"#endif\n"
"}"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2105
msgid "(Contributed by Eddie Elizondo in :issue:`35810`.)"
msgstr "(Prispela Eddie Elizondo v :issue:`35810`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2107
msgid ""
"The :c:macro:`Py_DEPRECATED()` macro has been implemented for MSVC. The "
"macro now must be placed before the symbol name."
msgstr ""
"Makro :c:macro:`Py_DEPRECATED()` bylo implementovano pro MSVC. Makro nyni "
"musi byt umisteno pred jmenem symbolu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2112
msgid "Py_DEPRECATED(3.8) PyAPI_FUNC(int) Py_OldFunction(void);"
msgstr "Py_DEPRECATED(3.8) PyAPI_FUNC(int) Py_OldFunction(void);"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2116
msgid "(Contributed by Zackery Spytz in :issue:`33407`.)"
msgstr "(Prispela Zackery Spytz v :issue:`33407`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2118
msgid ""
"The interpreter does not pretend to support binary compatibility of "
"extension types across feature releases, anymore.  A :c:type:`PyTypeObject` "
"exported by a third-party extension module is supposed to have all the slots"
" expected in the current Python version, including "
":c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_finalize` (:c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_FINALIZE` "
"is not checked anymore before reading "
":c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_finalize`)."
msgstr ""
"Interpret jiz nepredstira podporu binarni kompatibilite typu extension mezi "
"feature vydani. :c:type:`PyTypeObject` vyvezeny extension modulem tretich "
"stran je obsahovat vsechny sloty ocekavane v aktualni verzi Pythonu, vcetn "
":c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_finalize` (:c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_FINALIZE` "
"jiz neni kontrolovano pred ctenem :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_finalize`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2125
msgid "(Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`32388`.)"
msgstr "(Prispela Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`32388`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2127
msgid ""
"The functions :c:func:`!PyNode_AddChild` and :c:func:`!PyParser_AddToken` "
"now accept two additional ``int`` arguments *end_lineno* and "
"*end_col_offset*."
msgstr ""
"Funkce :c:func:`!PyNode_AddChild` a :c:func:`!PyParser_AddToken` nyn "
"akceptuji dva dodatecne ``int`` argumenty *end_lineno* a *end_col_offset*."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2130
msgid ""
"The :file:`libpython38.a` file to allow MinGW tools to link directly against"
" :file:`python38.dll` is no longer included in the regular Windows "
"distribution. If you require this file, it may be generated with the "
"``gendef`` and ``dlltool`` tools, which are part of the MinGW binutils "
"package:"
msgstr ""
"Soubor :file:`libpython38.a` umoznit MinGW nastroju priamo připojit proti "
":file:`python38.dll` jiz neni zahrnut v normalni Windows distribuci. Pokud "
"potrebujete tento soubor, muze byt generovan s ``gendef`` a ``dlltool`` "
"nastroji, ktere jsou soucasti MinGW binutils baliku:"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2135
msgid ""
"gendef - python38.dll > tmp.def\n"
"dlltool --dllname python38.dll --def tmp.def --output-lib libpython38.a"
msgstr ""
"gendef - python38.dll > tmp.def\n"
"dlltool --dllname python38.dll --def tmp.def --output-lib libpython38.a"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2140
msgid ""
"The location of an installed :file:`pythonXY.dll` will depend on the "
"installation options and the version and language of Windows. See "
":ref:`using-on-windows` for more information. The resulting library should "
"be placed in the same directory as :file:`pythonXY.lib`, which is generally "
"the :file:`libs` directory under your Python installation."
msgstr ""
"Umisteni instalovaneho :file:`pythonXY.dll` bude zaviset na moznostech "
"instalace a verze a jazyce Windows. Viz :ref:`using-on-windows` pro vice "
"informaci. Vysledna knihovna by mela byt umistena ve stejnem adresari jako "
":file:`pythonXY.lib`, coz je obecne :file:`libs` adresar pod vasim "
"instalacnim Python."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2146
msgid "(Contributed by Steve Dower in :issue:`37351`.)"
msgstr "(Prispela Steve Dower v :issue:`37351`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2150
msgid "CPython bytecode changes"
msgstr "CPython bytecode zmeny"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2152
msgid ""
"The interpreter loop  has been simplified by moving the logic of unrolling "
"the stack of blocks into the compiler.  The compiler emits now explicit "
"instructions for adjusting the stack of values and calling the cleaning-up "
"code for :keyword:`break`, :keyword:`continue` and :keyword:`return`."
msgstr ""
"Smycka interprete byla zjednodusena presunem logiky rozmotavani zasobnika "
"bloku do kompilatoru. Kompilatr nyn vysila explicitni instrukce pro "
"prislusnout zasobniku hodnot a volani cisti kodu pro :keyword:`break`, "
":keyword:`continue` a :keyword:`return`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2158
msgid ""
"Removed opcodes :opcode:`!BREAK_LOOP`, :opcode:`!CONTINUE_LOOP`, "
":opcode:`!SETUP_LOOP` and :opcode:`!SETUP_EXCEPT`.  Added new opcodes "
":opcode:`!ROT_FOUR`, :opcode:`!BEGIN_FINALLY`, :opcode:`!CALL_FINALLY` and "
":opcode:`!POP_FINALLY`.  Changed the behavior of :opcode:`!END_FINALLY` and "
":opcode:`!WITH_CLEANUP_START`."
msgstr ""
"Odstrany operacni kody :opcode:`!BREAK_LOOP`, :opcode:`!CONTINUE_LOOP`, "
":opcode:`!SETUP_LOOP` a :opcode:`!SETUP_EXCEPT`. Pridany nove operacni kody "
":opcode:`!ROT_FOUR`, :opcode:`!BEGIN_FINALLY`, :opcode:`!CALL_FINALLY` a "
":opcode:`!POP_FINALLY`. Zmenen chovani :opcode:`!END_FINALLY` a "
":opcode:`!WITH_CLEANUP_START`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2164
msgid ""
"(Contributed by Mark Shannon, Antoine Pitrou and Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`17611`.)"
msgstr ""
"(Prispeli Mark Shannon, Antoine Pitrou a Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`17611`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2167
msgid ""
"Added new opcode :opcode:`END_ASYNC_FOR` for handling exceptions raised when"
" awaiting a next item in an :keyword:`async for` loop. (Contributed by "
"Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`33041`.)"
msgstr ""
"Pridan novy opcode :opcode:`END_ASYNC_FOR` pro zpracovani vyjimek vyhozeny "
"pri cekani na dalsi prvek v :keyword:`async for` smyce. (Prispela Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`33041`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2171
msgid ""
"The :opcode:`MAP_ADD` now expects the value as the first element in the "
"stack and the key as the second element. This change was made so the key is "
"always evaluated before the value in dictionary comprehensions, as proposed "
"by :pep:`572`. (Contributed by Jörn Heissler in :issue:`35224`.)"
msgstr ""
":opcode:`MAP_ADD` nyní očekává hodnotu jako první prvek v zásobníku a klíč "
"jako druhý prvek. Tato změna byla provedena tak, aby byl klíč vždy "
"vyhodnocen před hodnotou v dictionary comprehension, jak je navrženo "
":pep:`572`. (Přispěl Jörn Heissler v :issue:`35224`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2178
msgid "Demos and Tools"
msgstr "Demo a Nastroje"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2180
msgid ""
"Added a benchmark script for timing various ways to access variables: "
"``Tools/scripts/var_access_benchmark.py``. (Contributed by Raymond Hettinger"
" in :issue:`35884`.)"
msgstr ""
"Pridan skript benchmarku pro casovani ruznych zposobu pristupu k promennym: "
"``Tools/scripts/var_access_benchmark.py``. (Prispela Raymond Hettinger v "
":issue:`35884`.)"

