#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2240
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.1"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.1"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2242
msgid ""
"Due to significant security concerns, the *reuse_address* parameter of "
":meth:`asyncio.loop.create_datagram_endpoint` is no longer supported. This "
"is because of the behavior of the socket option ``SO_REUSEADDR`` in UDP. For"
" more details, see the documentation for "
"``loop.create_datagram_endpoint()``. (Contributed by Kyle Stanley, Antoine "
"Pitrou, and Yury Selivanov in :issue:`37228`.)"
msgstr ""
"Kuli vyznamnym bezpecnostnim obavam, parametr *reuse_address* "
":meth:`asyncio.loop.create_datagram_endpoint` jiz neni podporovan. Je to "
"proto chovanis socketu volby ``SO_REUSEADDR`` v UDP. Pro vise detailu viz "
"dokumentace ``loop.create_datagram_endpoint()``. (Prispeli Kyle Stanley, "
"Antoine Pitrou a Yury Selivanov v :issue:`37228`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2250
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.2"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.2"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2252
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression with the ``ignore`` callback of :func:`shutil.copytree`. "
"The argument types are now str and List[str] again. (Contributed by Manuel "
"Barkhau and Giampaolo Rodola in :gh:`83571`.)"
msgstr ""
"Opravena regrese se ``ignore`` zpetnym volanim :func:`shutil.copytree`. Typy"
" argumentu jsou nyn str a List[str] znovu. (Prispeli Manuel Barkhau a "
"Giampaolo Rodola v :gh:`83571`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2257
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.3"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.3"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2259
msgid ""
"The constant values of future flags in the :mod:`__future__` module are "
"updated in order to prevent collision with compiler flags. Previously "
"``PyCF_ALLOW_TOP_LEVEL_AWAIT`` was clashing with ``CO_FUTURE_DIVISION``. "
"(Contributed by Batuhan Taskaya in :gh:`83743`)"
msgstr ""
"Konstantni hodnoty budoucich flagu v modulu :mod:`__future__` jsou "
"aktualizovany aby se zabranilo kolizi s vlajkami kompilatoru. Driveji "
"``PyCF_ALLOW_TOP_LEVEL_AWAIT`` srazovalo s ``CO_FUTURE_DIVISION``. (Prispela"
" Batuhan Taskaya v :gh:`83743`)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2265
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.8"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.8"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2267
msgid ""
"Earlier Python versions allowed using both ``;`` and ``&`` as query "
"parameter separators in :func:`urllib.parse.parse_qs` and "
":func:`urllib.parse.parse_qsl`.  Due to security concerns, and to conform "
"with newer W3C recommendations, this has been changed to allow only a single"
" separator key, with ``&`` as the default.  This change also affects "
":func:`!cgi.parse` and :func:`!cgi.parse_multipart` as they use the affected"
" functions internally. For more details, please see their respective "
"documentation. (Contributed by Adam Goldschmidt, Senthil Kumaran and Ken Jin"
" in :issue:`42967`.)"
msgstr ""
"Driveji Python verze umoznovaly pouziti jak ``;`` tak ``&`` jako oddelovat "
"parametru dotazu v :func:`urllib.parse.parse_qs` a "
":func:`urllib.parse.parse_qsl`. Kuli bezpecnostnim obavam a shodou s "
"novejsimi W3C doporucenims, toto bylo zmeneno aby umoznovalo pouze jeden "
"klic oddelovatele, s ``&`` jako vychozim. Tato zmena take ovlivnuje "
":func:`!cgi.parse` a :func:`!cgi.parse_multipart`, jelikoz interny pouzivaji"
" ovlivnene funkce. Pro vise detailu, prosim viz jejich respective "
"dokumentaci. (Prispeli Adam Goldschmidt, Senthil Kumaran a Ken Jin v "
":issue:`42967`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2278
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.9"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.9"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2280
msgid ""
"A security fix alters the :class:`ftplib.FTP` behavior to not trust the IPv4"
" address sent from the remote server when setting up a passive data channel."
"  We reuse the ftp server IP address instead.  For unusual code requiring "
"the old behavior, set a ``trust_server_pasv_ipv4_address`` attribute on your"
" FTP instance to ``True``.  (See :gh:`87451`)"
msgstr ""
"Oprava bezpecnosti meni chovanis :class:`ftplib.FTP` aby nedoverovalo IPv4 "
"adrese odesilane ze vzdaleneho serveru pri nastaveni pasivniho datoveho "
"kanalu. Preuzivame FTP server IP adresu miste. Pro neobycejny kod vyzadujici"
" stare chovanis, nastavte atribut ``trust_server_pasv_ipv4_address`` na "
"vasem FTP instanci na ``True``. (Viz :gh:`87451`)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2287 ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2307
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.10"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.10"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2290
msgid "macOS 11.0 (Big Sur) and Apple Silicon Mac support"
msgstr "macOS 11.0 (Big Sur) a Apple Silicon Mac popora"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2292
msgid ""
"As of 3.8.10, Python now supports building and running on macOS 11 (Big Sur)"
" and on Apple Silicon Macs (based on the ``ARM64`` architecture). A new "
"universal build variant, ``universal2``, is now available to natively "
"support both ``ARM64`` and ``Intel 64`` in one set of executables. Note that"
" support for \"weaklinking\", building binaries targeted for newer versions "
"of macOS that will also run correctly on older versions by testing at "
"runtime for missing features, is not included in this backport from Python "
"3.9; to support a range of macOS versions, continue to target for and build "
"on the oldest version in the range."
msgstr ""
"Od 3.8.10, Python nyn podporuje stavbu a spousteni na macOS 11 (Big Sur) a "
"na Apple Silicon Macech (na zaklade ``ARM64`` architektury). Nova "
"variantakonstrukce universal2 je nyn dostupna pro nativne podporu obou "
"``ARM64`` a ``Intel 64`` v jedne sadou spustiteln. Poznamejte, ze popora "
"\"weaklinkingu\", stavba binarni cilu pro novejsi verze macOS, ktere budou "
"take spravne spusteny na starsi verze testovanim za behm pro chybejici "
"funkce, neni zahrnuty v tomto backportu z Pythonu 3.9; pro podporu rozsahu "
"macOS verzi, pokracujte v cili a stavbe na nejstarsim verze v rozsahu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2302
msgid ""
"(Originally contributed by Ronald Oussoren and Lawrence D'Anna in "
":gh:`85272`, with fixes by FX Coudert and Eli Rykoff, and backported to 3.8 "
"by Maxime Bélanger and Ned Deily)"
msgstr ""
"(Puvne prispeli Ronald Oussoren a Lawrence D'Anna v :gh:`85272`, s opravami "
"od FX Coudert a Eli Rykoff a backportovano na 3.8 Maxime Belanger a Ned "
"Deily)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2310
msgid "urllib.parse"
msgstr "urllib.parse"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2312
msgid ""
"The presence of newline or tab characters in parts of a URL allows for some "
"forms of attacks. Following the WHATWG specification that updates "
":rfc:`3986`, ASCII newline ``\\n``, ``\\r`` and tab ``\\t`` characters are "
"stripped from the URL by the parser in :mod:`urllib.parse` preventing such "
"attacks. The removal characters are controlled by a new module level "
"variable ``urllib.parse._UNSAFE_URL_BYTES_TO_REMOVE``. (See :issue:`43882`)"
msgstr ""
"Pritomnost nove a karty znaku v castech URL umoznuje nektere formy utoku. "
"Nasledujici WHATWG specifikaci, ktera aktualizuje :rfc:`3986`, ASCII nova "
"radka ``\\n``, ``\\r`` a karty ``\\t`` znaky jsou odstrany z URL "
"analyzatorem v :mod:`urllib.parse` zabranujici takovym utokum. Odstraneni "
"znaky jsou rizeny novou modulem uroven promenne "
"``urllib.parse._UNSAFE_URL_BYTES_TO_REMOVE``. (Viz :issue:`43882`)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2321
msgid "Notable changes in Python 3.8.12"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v Pythonu 3.8.12"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2326
msgid ""
"Starting with Python 3.8.12 the :mod:`ipaddress` module no longer accepts "
"any leading zeros in IPv4 address strings. Leading zeros are ambiguous and "
"interpreted as octal notation by some libraries. For example the legacy "
"function :func:`socket.inet_aton` treats leading zeros as octal notation. "
"glibc implementation of modern :func:`~socket.inet_pton` does not accept any"
" leading zeros."
msgstr ""
"Pocina s Pythonem 3.8.12 modul :mod:`ipaddress` jiz neakceptuje zadne "
"predhodni nuly v IPv4 adrese retezci. Predhodni nuly jsou nejasne a "
"interpretovany jako oktal zapis nekterymi knihovnami. Naprklad dedictvi "
"funkce :func:`socket.inet_aton` zach az predhodni nuly jako oktal zapis. "
"glibc implementace modernich :func:`~socket.inet_pton` neprijima zadne "
"predhodni nuly."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2333
msgid ""
"(Originally contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`36384`, and "
"backported to 3.8 by Achraf Merzouki.)"
msgstr ""
"(Puvne prispela Christian Heimes v :issue:`36384` a backportovano na 3.8 "
"Achraf Merzouki.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2337
msgid "Notable security feature in 3.8.14"
msgstr "Vyrazna bezpecnostni funkcnost v 3.8.14"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2339
msgid ""
"Converting between :class:`int` and :class:`str` in bases other than 2 "
"(binary), 4, 8 (octal), 16 (hexadecimal), or 32 such as base 10 (decimal) "
"now raises a :exc:`ValueError` if the number of digits in string form is "
"above a limit to avoid potential denial of service attacks due to the "
"algorithmic complexity. This is a mitigation for :cve:`2020-10735`. This "
"limit can be configured or disabled by environment variable, command line "
"flag, or :mod:`sys` APIs. See the :ref:`integer string conversion length "
"limitation <int_max_str_digits>` documentation.  The default limit is 4300 "
"digits in string form."
msgstr ""
"Konverze mezi :class:`int` a :class:`str` v zakladech jine nez 2 (binarni), "
"4, 8 (oktal), 16 (hexadecimalni) nebo 32, jako je zaklad 10 (dekadni), nyn "
"vyhodi :exc:`ValueError`, pokud je pocet cifer v retezci forma vyse limit "
"aby se zabranilo potencialnim utokum odmitnutu sluzby kv kuli algoritmicke "
"slozitosti. Toto je zmirnovani pro :cve:`2020-10735`. Tento limit muze byt "
"konfigurovan nebo vypnut pomoci promenne prostredi, vlajky prikazoveho radku"
" nebo :mod:`sys` API. Viz :ref:`integer string conversion length limitation "
"<int_max_str_digits>` dokumentaci. Vychozi limit je 4300 cifer v retezci "
"forma."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2350
msgid "Notable changes in 3.8.17"
msgstr "Vyrazne zmeny v 3.8.17"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:2355
msgid ""
"The extraction methods in :mod:`tarfile`, and :func:`shutil.unpack_archive`,"
" have a new a *filter* argument that allows limiting tar features than may "
"be surprising or dangerous, such as creating files outside the destination "
"directory. See :ref:`tarfile-extraction-filter` for details. In Python 3.12,"
" use without the *filter* argument will show a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. In"
" Python 3.14, the default will switch to ``'data'``. (Contributed by Petr "
"Viktorin in :pep:`706`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metody extrakce v :mod:`tarfile` a :func:`shutil.unpack_archive` maji nove "
"argument *filter*, ktery umoznuje omezeni tar vlastnosti nez mohou byt "
"prekvapive nebo nebezpecne, jako je vytvareni souboru mimo cilovy adresar. "
"Viz :ref:`tarfile-extraction-filter` pro detaily. V Pythonu 3.12, pouziti "
"bez *filter* argumentu bude zobrazit :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. V Pythonu "
"3.14, vychozim se prepne na ``'data'``. (Prispela Petr Viktorin v "
":pep:`706`.)"

